// With die_with_parent, a child the program doesn't wait for ends when the program does:
// on Linux PR_SET_PDEATHSIG, on Windows a Job Object that ends it when it is closed.
// The program starts a child that runs for a minute, says so, and ends without waiting for
// it. The child is tests/helpers/child.ctx, as `beat_aloud PATH`: it makes the file PATH
// grow, and prints `beating`.
// That the child has ended is the file no longer growing (`ends PATH`).
//# only: windows linux: macOS has no way for a child to end with its parent
//# build child: {home}/tests/helpers/child.ctx
//# build program: main.ctx
//# make dir beat
//# $ {program} {child} true beat/file
//# timeout: 30
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| beating
//# $ {child} ends beat/file
//# exit: 0
//# stdout:
//| ended
